1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,908
Asking Questions at a Trade Fair At a fair a producer displayed

2
00:00:04,921 --> 00:00:10,158
a prototype with a patent application pending Its spokesman praised an ingenious

3
00:00:10,171 --> 00:00:15,710
modification that could halve processing time I asked for the specification the

4
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:21,447
conditions of the comparison and a demonstration using an ordinary workpiece The

5
00:00:21,461 --> 00:00:25,776
machine had a modular design one module could detach from another and

6
00:00:25,789 --> 00:00:30,513
a handy fitting allowed adjustment A cutter moved along a preset track

7
00:00:30,526 --> 00:00:35,197
while a roller guided the material The output looked first-rate but the

8
00:00:35,211 --> 00:00:41,237
representative admitted that a delicate garment required different settings A promotional claim

9
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:46,724
needed qualification We discussed a possible deal without making an immediate bid

10
00:00:47,632 --> 00:00:51,684
A clear quotation would identify what the price included what support was

11
00:00:51,697 --> 00:00:56,934
available and who would be liable if delivery failed Commercial courtesy does

12
00:00:56,947 --> 00:01:02,855
not require unquestioning acceptance A buyer can remain gracious while asking firm

13
00:01:03,013 --> 00:01:06,079
pertinent questions about a product's actual performance
